       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. Even if both are accurate, 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled dose, and I don't know of any evidence that it's safe. The risks include GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove them.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum:** for example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day). I can add a note that the specialist has recommended a higher dose and that it needs review.\n- **Hold the order** while you contact the specialist and pharmacy. They can confirm the dose directly and decide whether to enter or override it through their own process.\n- **Look at alternatives:** if standard NSAID dosing failed, the specialist may want a different drug or an adjunct, rather than a supratherapeutic ibuprofen dose.\n\nTell me which of these you want. If you want the 800 mg option, I'll enter it now."
